# NeXuS Web Server — project-local secrets (.local.env)
#
# Copy to ".local.env" (same folder as your project / next to the server / your CWD) and
# fill in real keys. This file OVERRIDES ~/.config/nexus/secrets/nexus.env for this project.
#
# Precedence (highest first):  process-env  >  .local.env  >  nexus.env  >  legacy pollinations.key
#
# Security (handled for you):
#   • never web-served    — the static server hard-refuses any .env/.key/.pem/dotfile (404)
#   • never git-committed  — the server auto-adds these to a .gitignore in this folder on startup
#   • never logged/returned — keys are injected into upstream calls only; /api/providers is booleans-only
#   • recommended:  chmod 600 .local.env
#
# Only set the providers you actually use. Keyless providers (aihorde/ollama/aichat) need nothing here.

# ── Keys for BUILT-IN providers ───────────────────────────────────────────────
POLLINATIONS_API_KEY=sk_your_pollinations_key_here
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk_your_openai_key_here
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=your_mistral_key_here
# GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key_here
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your_openrouter_key_here

# ── Declare a WHOLE NEW provider from here — no code edit (universal API server) ─
# The proxy scans for PROVIDER_<ID>_BASE_URL and registers <id> on the fly; it then
# appears in /api/providers and the app's provider dropdown, and is callable at
# POST /api/llm/<id>/v1/chat/completions  (OpenAI-compatible; key injected server-side).
#
#   PROVIDER_<ID>_BASE_URL   (required)  e.g. https://host/v1   — makes <id> exist
#   PROVIDER_<ID>_API_KEY    (optional)  present → key-required; absent → keyless
#   PROVIDER_<ID>_KIND       (optional)  chat | image | chat+image   (default chat)
#   PROVIDER_<ID>_LABEL      (optional)  friendly name for the UI
#
# Example — a local vLLM/LM-Studio/OpenAI-compatible box:
# PROVIDER_MYLLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# PROVIDER_MYLLM_API_KEY=sk-local
# PROVIDER_MYLLM_KIND=chat
# PROVIDER_MYLLM_LABEL=My Local LLM
